  1250	### 8.5 Macro declarations travel beside the tree
  1251	
  1252	The `:macro?` flag is outside the canonical tree (§2.5). What replaces it
  1253	is a **declaration fact bound to an occurrence**, produced by the frontend
  1254	and consumed by the expander at admission. The governing contract admits
  1255	and harvests **every entity in the batch, in batch order, including
  1256	definitions disconnected from the execution root**
  1257	(`yin.vm.macro.md:229-249`). A single rooted tree cannot carry a
  1258	disconnected definition, so the composition between frontend and expander
  1259	is an **ordered batch**, not a tree:
  1260	
  1261	```clojure
  1262	{:yin/batch         [<tree-0> <tree-1> … <tree-n>]   ; canonical trees, one per admitted root or disconnected subgraph
  1263	 :yin/root          i                                ; index of the tree the evaluator runs
  1264	 :yin/declarations  #{[j path :yin.macro/definition] …}   ; the definition at path in tree j is a macro
  1265	 :yin/harvest       [#{[j path] …} #{[j' path'] …} …]}   ; one entry per ORIGINAL definition, in admission order;
  1266	                                                     ;   each entry is the set of [j path] occurrences of that definition
  1267	```
